---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  alternateHref="/"
  title="VietWireless | Visual notes on wireless communications"
  description="Visual explanations of signals, wireless communications, OFDM, 5G NR, NTN and 6G, with engineering intuition and interactive examples."
>
  <article class="home-essay shell">
    <header class="essay-hero">
      <p class="chapter-label">VIETWIRELESS · CHAPTER 0</p>
      <h1>
        Before 5G, start with a simpler question:
        <br />
        <em>how do we send information over distance?</em>
      </h1>
      <p class="essay-lead">
        Wireless communications is easier to understand when the ideas are connected:
        a physical waveform, sampling, frequency, complex baseband, modulation, OFDM,
        the radio channel and finally the structures used by 4G, 5G NR and NTN.
      </p>

    </header>

    <section class="essay-section" id="history">
      <div class="section-number">01</div>
      <div class="essay-content">
        <p class="section-kicker">THE LONG VIEW</p>
        <h2>Different generations of communication systems keep solving the same core problem.</h2>
        <p>
          Information must be represented by a signal, transported through a physical channel,
          observed in noise and reconstructed at the receiver. Radio technology changes quickly;
          these foundations do not.
        </p>

        <div class="history-overview" aria-label="A compact history of communications">
          <div class="history-overview-track" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="history-overview-item"><time>1864</time><i></i><strong>Theory</strong><span>Electromagnetic waves</span></div>
          <div class="history-overview-item"><time>1901</time><i></i><strong>Wireless</strong><span>Radio telegraphy</span></div>
          <div class="history-overview-item"><time>1948</time><i></i><strong>Information</strong><span>Bits · noise · capacity</span></div>
          <div class="history-overview-item"><time>1979</time><i></i><strong>Cellular</strong><span>Spectrum reuse</span></div>
          <div class="history-overview-item"><time>Today</time><i></i><strong>5G / NTN</strong><span>Modern radio networks</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="essay-section" id="big-picture">
      <div class="section-number">02</div>
      <div class="essay-content">
        <p class="section-kicker">THE BIG PICTURE</p>
        <h2>Follow one signal from information to RF, through the channel, and back again.</h2>
        <p>
          The learning map starts with what a signal is, then moves through sampling,
          amplitude/frequency/phase, complex numbers, I and Q, Fourier analysis, modulation,
          the wireless channel, OFDM, resource grids and 5G NR.
        </p>

        <div class="teaching-steps">
          <article><span>01</span><h3>Signal foundations</h3><p>Time, frequency, samples, phase, complex numbers and I and Q.</p></article>
          <article><span>02</span><h3>Wireless link</h3><p>RF, antennas, noise, multipath, fading and synchronization.</p></article>
          <article><span>03</span><h3>OFDM</h3><p>Subcarriers, FFT/IFFT, cyclic prefix and the resource grid.</p></article>
          <article><span>04</span><h3>5G NR & NTN</h3><p>Initial access, channels, reference signals, timing and satellite effects.</p></article>
        </div>

        <a class="text-button" href="/en/learn/">Open the learning map →</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="start-card">
      <p class="chapter-label">START HERE</p>
      <h2>Learn the system in the order the concepts depend on one another.</h2>
      <p>
        The English edition is being introduced progressively. The bilingual structure is now in place,
        with the full Vietnamese lessons remaining available while English lesson translations are added.
      </p>
      <a class="text-button" href="/en/learn/">Open the learning map →</a>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
